    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POSITIVE PAIRS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pairs of data points known to be alike or from the same class, used as references for contrastive learning during training."&lt;SEP&gt;"Positive pairs are specific instances utilized during CLIP training aimed to enhance model performance by optimizing their dot products."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term 'positive pairs' refers to grouped data points that share certain characteristics or are related in some way."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b51c9e3439fc588a037c55333c86c6cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de49685904c478fbf8cf8050f3485fb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
