    <node id="&quot;TRANSFORMERS AND SELF-ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transformers are neural network architectures that use self-attention mechanisms instead of recurrent layers, making them faster for sequence-to-sequence tasks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transformers use self-attention mechanisms instead of RNNs for sequence-to-sequence tasks"</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-023c8b67da94a3b9edf077fa3025ccbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db09b94e4d3bf6b9793eca0b3d3ef219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SINGLE-HEAD SELF-ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A simplified version of multi-headed attention that processes only one context at a time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Single-head self-attention refers to a model with one head for attention computation, which is less complex compared to multi-head versions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Self-attention with a single attention head reduces the computational complexity in transformer-based models."&lt;SEP&gt;"A technique in natural language processing and deep learning that allows models to weigh the importance of different elements within a sequence of inputs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-023c8b67da94a3b9edf077fa3025ccbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99819c35bbf0101274afb02fb3b32d83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c87cd3d29a0304bd90833bfc5ea711a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db09b94e4d3bf6b9793eca0b3d3ef219</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 22}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTI-HEAD SELF-ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Combines multiple single-head attentions to weigh different contexts effectively"&lt;SEP&gt;"Multi-head self-attention uses multiple heads in parallel to process different aspects of the input data, enhancing computational efficiency and representational power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Multi-head self-attention is an extension of self-attention that uses multiple parallel attention mechanisms to improve model performance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-023c8b67da94a3b9edf077fa3025ccbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db09b94e4d3bf6b9793eca0b3d3ef219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c87cd3d29a0304bd90833bfc5ea711a5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULTILAYER PERCEPTRON (MLP)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A Multilayer Perceptron is a feedforward artificial neural network consisting of multiple layers of perceptrons with nonlinear activation functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"A neural network architecture used for various machine learning tasks including language processing."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Multilayer Perceptron is a type of feedforward artificial neural network that consists of multiple layers of nodes, in which each layer fully connects to the next one. It's used for several tasks like pattern recognition and classification."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-023c8b67da94a3b9edf077fa3025ccbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db09b94e4d3bf6b9793eca0b3d3ef219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47347221c55bcc8f1856d45da47afe2e</data>
