    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D_Q&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'d_q' represents the number of dimensions across which embedding is performed, referring to a concept in vector space projection."&lt;SEP&gt;"'d_q' specifies the dimensionality of matrix W^q, indicating how many query features or dimensions each token can have."&lt;SEP&gt;"d_q refers to the dimension 'd' when calculating query vectors, which needs to match with d_k for proper dot product calculation."&lt;SEP&gt;"d_q represents dimensions used in calculating the query and key vectors."&lt;SEP&gt;"The dimensions \(d\) mentioned are spatial dimensions and play a role in calculating query and key vectors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32e51673be16864652dbab8fc07a061e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 45}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D_K&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'d_k' indicates the dimensionality of matrix W^k which is equivalent to 'd_q', reflecting that queries and keys occupy typically the same dimensional space in these models."&lt;SEP&gt;"d_k represents dimensions used in calculations when projecting tokens into a new space for forming generalized dot product."&lt;SEP&gt;"Similar to \(d_q\), \(d_k\) also refers to dimensions, used specifically for calculating the dot product between query and key vectors."&lt;SEP&gt;"'d_k' represents the number of dimensions for calculating query and key vectors, another dimensionality term related to vector space manipulation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32e51673be16864652dbab8fc07a061e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 6}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 45}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;D_V&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"'d_v' denotes the dimensionality of matrix W^v, specifying how many value features or dimensions each token has during the embedding process."&lt;SEP&gt;"d_v denotes the dimensionality of the value space where input tokens are projected for updating their embeddings."&lt;SEP&gt;"The value space dimensionality represented by \(d_v\) indicates an organization's configuration for handling information dimensions in computations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de442a5e4162d7683f6a2442131b7161&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e51673be16864652dbab8fc07a061e</data>
