    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRESENTATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Encoded vector outputs of a model or encoder; in contrastive learning, they are optimized to be close for positive pairs and apart for negative pairs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Representations are created by data processing techniques and should ideally be invariant to certain transformations when employing contrastive learning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-124fbb1b8e31d8533b54ab785a1c693b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VAE ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"This is a reference to variational autoencoder architecture, which might be another topic covered in discussions about generative models or machine learning. It could refer to architectural details related to VAEs."&lt;SEP&gt;"VAE (Variational Autoencoder) is a type of architecture used in machine learning for unsupervised dimensionality reduction and generative modeling."&lt;SEP&gt;"VAE Architecture focuses on the engineering of AI agents and is deeply involved in AI fields like deep networks, perception, kinematics, state estimation, large language models, multimodal reasoning, task planning, global and local planning, Markov decision processes, reinforcement learning, VLA Agents, Generative Modeling, Variational Inference, Expectation - Maximization (EM) Algorithm, Variational AutoEncoder - Keras, Variational Autoencoder from Scratch - Torch Stable Diffusion Playground, and Stable Diffusion Part 1. It offers courses on Introduction to AI and AI for Robotics as well as Deep Learning for Computer Vision and Data Mining that's being ported."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f6641e40121bf773ff57d0a659c229b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e5ce531950e2a80d0c630acc2dcd351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086978ab1a823b35a328c5fd09b9549c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 59}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PGM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PGM (Probabilistic Graphical Model) is a framework for representing complex probability distributions and performing inference on those distributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086978ab1a823b35a328c5fd09b9549c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 59}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DNN_ENC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DNN_enc (Deep Neural Network encoder) is an architecture used in machine learning that processes input data and extracts meaningful features, which are then encoded into compact representations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086978ab1a823b35a328c5fd09b9549c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 58}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Μ, LOG Σ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"μ (mu), log Σ (log Sigma) denote statistical parameters in the context of probabilistic models like VAEs. μ represents the mean vector that indicates the central tendency of a distribution while log Σ relates to the precision matrix or variance of the Gaussian distributions used for approximations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-086978ab1a823b35a328c5fd09b9549c</data>
      <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 58}]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;N(&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"N (Gaussian function) is used in probability theory and statistics as it models continuous data with normal distributions, providing a basis for probabilistic calculations like those performed by DNN_enc and μ, log Σ."</data>
