    <node id="&quot;REPRESENTATIONAL COLLAPSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A phenomenon where a model maps all inputs into the same or very similar representations which can lead to poor performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Representational collapse refers to the situation where a model maps all inputs into the same vector, essentially losing its ability to distinguish between different inputs."&lt;SEP&gt;"A phenomenon where machine learning models simplify their representations, often mapping all data points to identical vectors, leading to a loss of information."&lt;SEP&gt;"Representational collapse" refers to the issue where all data points are represented in a single, uniform way instead of capturing the nuances of individual data points."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
