    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;CLUSTERING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning might seem unrelated at first but shares similarities with clustering when dealing with similar data points mapping to embeddings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-575b5e50472741efa7a02966c34ea787</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;NEGATIVE PAIRS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Negative pairs serve as inputs in contrastive learning where their embeddings are expected to differ significantly in \(z\)-space, typically constructed randomly."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c0d666dc2b38320dbc3e9ac039241910</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;SUPERVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning uses supervision in the form of positive and negative pairs, guiding the model on what representations are similar or distinct."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c0d666dc2b38320dbc3e9ac039241910</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;\(\MATHBF{X}\)&quot;, &quot;\(\MATHBF{X}^{+}\)&quot;, &quot;\(\MATHBF{X}^{-}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In contrastive learning, data points \(\mathbf{x}\), their transformations \(\mathbf{x}^{+}\) under \(T()\), and negative pairs \(\mathbf{x}^-\) are used to guide the learning of representations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c0d666dc2b38320dbc3e9ac039241910</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;AN INFORMATION BOTTLENECK&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The concept of an information bottleneck relates to the limitations contrastive learning aims to overcome in data representation and compression."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-124fbb1b8e31d8533b54ab785a1c693b</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;CLIP ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"CLIP is specifically formulated as a contrastive learning method using visual and linguistic inputs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The CLIP architecture explicit decomposes contrastive learning into parts for alignment and uniformity, providing a methodological basis for this task."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-71e7394bf92a7151b6b24f6089eb88b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89614d99cc7b78ccf3cdf366b2958e93</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;V_1&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"V_1 contributes to contrastive learning by transforming data into different views, facilitating understanding through contrasting perspectives."&lt;SEP&gt;"V_1's application involves two types of contrastive learning, which are essentially the same process when viewed from different angles or perspectives."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cfbbffe94e6225bcf5568fe62c9c2cc2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;ALIGNMENT LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">70.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Alignment loss is one component of the Contrastive learning framework aimed at promoting similarity between related data points and distinguishing dissimilar ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alignment loss is part of contrastive learning framework designed to prevent representational collapse."&lt;SEP&gt;"An alignment loss is used in contrastive learning which aims to push apart embeddings of similar datapoints and align those of dissimilar ones."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrastive learning utilizes the alignment loss to correct representational collapse in machine learning models by pushing apart embeddings of different data points."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrastive learning employs the alignment loss to address issues with representational collapse and ensure embeddings from similar data points are distinct."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alignment loss is part of contrastive learning's mechanism for ensuring that similar data points are represented similarly."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrastive learning utilizes an alignment loss in conjunction with another one to prevent representational collapse and ensure differentiation of data points"&lt;SEP&gt;"Contrastive learning utilizes both alignment losses and another type of loss function that promotes embeddings of similar data points closer together while pushing apart those that are dissimilar, addressing issues like representational collapse."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;V_1(&lt;\MATHBF{X}&gt;)&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The application of contrastive learning involves comparing or contrasting different transformations or views generated from \(\mathbf{X}\), aiding in understanding similarities and differences within the same dataset."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cfbbffe94e6225bcf5568fe62c9c2cc2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;FIXING ISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning addresses the issue of trivial alignment by coupling with another loss function that separates embeddings of similar and dissimilar data points."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;ALIGNMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning uses alignments to distinguish between similar and dissimilar data points during training."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;PUSHING APART EMBEDDINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning's second loss component pushes apart the embeddings of negative pairs (dissimilar data) to enhance representation learning."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;COUPLES WITH&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The method couples an alignment loss with a 'pushing apart' loss for negative pairs to refine representation learning during training."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIONAL COLLAPSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning addresses the problem of representational collapse by pushing apart representations of different data points, thus distinguishing them."&lt;SEP&gt;"The purpose of contrastive learning is to prevent representational collapse by pushing apart the embeddings of similar and dissimilar data points."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;HYPERSPHERE METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Contrastive learning methodology is sometimes associated with or used alongside the Hypersphere method for representation learning tasks."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;DEEP LEARNING MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning can be applied in deep learning models to improve their performance by focusing on the differences between data points."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATION OPTIMIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive learning optimizes data representations by distinguishing between different instances of the same class, thus overcoming representational collapse"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
