      <data key="d6">chunk-3e73d0ea822bd93892030b14ea442531</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERATIVE MODEL&quot;" target="&quot;LATENT SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The generative model uses latent spaces to facilitate the creation of new instances that resemble the training dataset."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3e73d0ea822bd93892030b14ea442531</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERATIVE MODEL&quot;" target="&quot;PRIOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The prior plays a role in the generative process by providing an initial perspective that gets updated to form the posterior."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3e73d0ea822bd93892030b14ea442531</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INPUT EMBEDDING MATRIX&quot;" target="&quot;QUERY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Input Embedding Matrix is used to project inputs into the Query space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9526da303b971a977195d19a3809b3ae</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INPUT EMBEDDING MATRIX&quot;" target="&quot;KEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The same Input Embedding Matrix projects inputs into both Query and Key spaces, facilitating understanding of similarities."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9526da303b971a977195d19a3809b3ae</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INPUT EMBEDDING MATRIX&quot;" target="&quot;VALUES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The Input Embedding Matrix also projects input tokens into the Values space for retrieval or aggregation operations during computations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9526da303b971a977195d19a3809b3ae</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;KEY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Query and key are used in conjunction during tensor operations such as BMM and attention scores calculation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-57b7f9b1883ddd19c8bacc6f13c7a23a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;SCALED_DOT_PRODUCT_ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Query interacts directly with 'scaled_dot_product_attention' function to produce scores which are then used in the overall computation process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5fc28e3fa1a335ecb12a2c46fcb3980</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;SCORES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The change of the query leads to specific score values which are used to calculate matrix S."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5e821bceca23e38586c728f7eb2311c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;SOFTMAX FUNCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The query is processed through the softmax function to determine weights for different input elements."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5e821bceca23e38586c728f7eb2311c5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;EMBEDDING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The relationship between embedding processes and queries refers to how queries interact with transformed data representations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;KEY VECTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A query interacts with key vectors during the retrieval or calculation process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;KEYS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"There is a relationship between query and keys where a token performs both functions simultaneously. A token can seek (query) for other functions and express its own function (key)."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fe423a0387274e65441b9c527e0e5b66</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;CALCULATE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The action taken by the query vector during its interaction with key vectors."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY&quot;" target="&quot;MATRIX \(W^Q&quot;">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Matrix \(W^q\) is used in creating query vectors which are then compared or matched against key vectors for information retrieval or processing operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Matrix \(W^q\) might be related to the process of creating or utilizing queries involving \(W^v\), particularly in contexts where information retrieval or processing across multiple dimensions is involved."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bbe1fa761a3018b797f95e8931d7781d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VALUES&quot;" target="&quot;EMBEDDING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Values are derived from the input tokens and play a critical role in updating their embeddings during processing. The \(W^v\) matrix facilitates this transformation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-de442a5e4162d7683f6a2442131b7161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
