      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The action 'at' indicates that p1's airplane is located at LHR airport."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-96acc8ecd7298f81cb0386fe6d9bbcaf</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LLAVA&quot;" target="&quot;VISUAL INSTRUCTION TUNING&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"LLaVa is specifically designed for visual instruction tuning, leveraging multimodal reasoning capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c87cd3d29a0304bd90833bfc5ea711a5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CLASSIFICATION PROBLEM&quot;" target="&quot;INFONCE LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"InfoNCE loss is a method that treats establishing contrast as a classification problem."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-175a5eea9d1d7e4ef439a66c7ccf14ba</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INFONCE LOSS&quot;" target="&quot;CONTRASTIVE LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Contrastive Loss shares similarities with InfoNCE as both aim to enhance feature representation through contrasting positive and negative samples. However, InfoNCE specifically applies these principles within an unsupervised setting using information theory."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d356877d93c7363ed999b7b161849f6f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INFONCE LOSS&quot;" target="&quot;TRIPLET LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"While Triplet Loss focuses on distance-based comparisons with explicit margins to separate positive and negative pairs, InfoNCE extends the concept into unsupervised learning by leveraging mutual information between data points"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d356877d93c7363ed999b7b161849f6f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INFONCE LOSS&quot;" target="&quot;OOD2018REPRESENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The InfoNCE loss could be a theoretical or practical outcome related to the concept of ood2018representation, indicating an application or advancement in representation learning methods."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d356877d93c7363ed999b7b161849f6f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TORCH&quot;" target="&quot;F&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The torch organization includes a component named F which provides functionality related to operations like softmax."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-57b7f9b1883ddd19c8bacc6f13c7a23a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TORCH&quot;" target="&quot;SCALED_DOT_PRODUCT_ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The function 'scaled_dot_product_attention' uses functionalities from torch, including BMM and softmax."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5fc28e3fa1a335ecb12a2c46fcb3980</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;SCALED_DOT_PRODUCT_ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The function 'scaled_dot_product_attention' utilizes functions from F (torch.nn.functional), enhancing its computational capabilities."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5fc28e3fa1a335ecb12a2c46fcb3980</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;ALIGNMENT_LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The encoder 'f' is intended to learn in such a way that it becomes invariant to certain transformations \(T\) of input data, which requires minimizing the alignment loss."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;ZERO_VECTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"There's a risk of 'f' learning to output a zero vector as its result, leading to trivial alignment and representational collapse."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIONAL_COLLAPSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In representational collapse, encoder 'f' maps all input data into a single vector, which can result in trivial alignment and loss of discriminative power."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Encoder 'f' maps the input data into representations or embeddings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F&quot;" target="&quot;REPRESENTATIONAL COLLAPSE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The risk of representational collapse is mitigated through the use of contrastive learning, ensuring that similar data points are encoded differently despite being subject to same transformations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DIM_K&quot;" target="&quot;VARIABLE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Dim_k represents the dimension of query, affecting the scaling factor and behavior in the scaled dot product attention formula."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5fc28e3fa1a335ecb12a2c46fcb3980</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KEY&quot;" target="&quot;SCALED_DOT_PRODUCT_ATTENTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Key works in conjunction with query and value within 'scaled_dot_product_attention', influencing its outcome through specific operations."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5fc28e3fa1a335ecb12a2c46fcb3980</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KEY&quot;" target="&quot;MATRIX \(W^K)">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Matrix \(W^k\) is used in creating key vectors which are part of information processing systems that utilize keys for operations like attention and similarity scoring."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bbe1fa761a3018b797f95e8931d7781d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
