    <edge source="&quot;REBECA&quot;" target="&quot;USER INTERFACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The User Interface in Rebeca includes a chat application that allows text input and answer output, excluding specific interfaces or AI browsers."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c89dcb0ccedaa26a07f86fea9098be0f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;UI&quot;" target="&quot;SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The System Architecture of Rebeca includes the User Interface component, which is crucial for facilitating interactions with users."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b85eb0621a346e492e81a88a6d9f5d88</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;W^QX_I AND W^KX_J&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The specific elements operated on within the generalized dot product calculation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;THE EVOLVED DOT PRODUCT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The 'evolved' dot product refers to an advanced version of the generalized method."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;QUERY VECTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The generalized dot product operation is performed between the 'Wx' result (query vector) and 'Wx' of another entity in its new space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;KEY VECTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Similarly, the 'generalized dot product' is also computed between this query vector and a 'key vector', facilitating the matching process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;VECTOR SPACE CALCULATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The generalized dot product falls under vector space calculations after token projection."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT&quot;" target="&quot;PROJECTED TOKENS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The generalized dot product is applied to projected tokens in their new space, affecting the overall computational process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY-KEY SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;TRAINING PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The training process involves keys moving close to the queries in their respective dimensional spaces, impacting how they interact within this space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY-KEY SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;PROJECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Data transformation technique that places query and key vectors into a dimensionally aligned space for operation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;QUERY-KEY SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;W^Q&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Matrix W raised to qth power relates to operations performed on query vectors within their respective spaces."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PROJECTION&quot;" target="&quot;W^V MATRIX&quot;">
      <data key="d4">1.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The \(W^v\) matrix performs the projection operation on input tokens, which is essential for mapping them into value space."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-de442a5e4162d7683f6a2442131b7161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PROJECTION&quot;" target="&quot;WEIGHTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A projection with proper weights can cause mappings in the embedding space. The weights influence how different dimensions of the input data are emphasized or suppressed."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bbe1fa761a3018b797f95e8931d7781d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PROJECTION&quot;" target="&quot;EMBEDDING SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The goal of projections and weight adjustments during training is to map high-dimensional data into a lower space while preserving necessary information for tasks like similarity search."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bbe1fa761a3018b797f95e8931d7781d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INPUT TOKENS&quot;" target="&quot;\(W^V\) MATRIX&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Input tokens are transformed by the \(W^v\) matrix to produce value vectors."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-de442a5e4162d7683f6a2442131b7161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ZERO VECTOR&quot;" target="&quot;DATAPOINTS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In the context of representational collapse, datapoints get mapped to a zero vector which trivially satisfies alignment."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;W^Q&quot;" target="&quot;W^K&quot;">
      <data key="d4">13.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The relationship between 'W^q' and 'W^k' indicates their parallel role in facilitating the dot product computation, suggesting they are integral parts of the neural network or computational framework involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"W^q interacts with W^k for forming generalized dot product between query and key vectors during their matching process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ALIGNMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ENCODER F&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The alignment loss enforces that the encoder 'f' produces similar representations for inputs undergoing the same transformation 'T', thereby ensuring invariance."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SENSORY CO-OCCURRENCES&quot;" target="&quot;VIEWS OF \(\MATHBF{X}\)&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The process of creating multiple views of \(\mathbf{X}\) is based on the co-occurrence of sensory data or features within the dataset."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cfbbffe94e6225bcf5568fe62c9c2cc2</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KEY SPACE&quot;" target="&quot;VALUE SPACE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Key and value spaces interact in multi-dimensional operations to compute attentions and update embeddings."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-de442a5e4162d7683f6a2442131b7161</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;W^Q, W^K&quot;" target="&quot;TOKEN TRANSFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"These matrices are used to transform tokens into their respective new spaces."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GENERALIZED DOT PRODUCT WX_J&quot;" target="&quot;VISUALIZE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The concept explained through a graphical representation of token transformation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CHANGE&quot;" target="&quot;QUERY-KEY INTERACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Change is a result of query-key interactions during the training process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;REPRESENTATIONAL_COLLAPSE&quot;" target="&quot;ISSUE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The issue of representational collapse, where 'f' maps all data points to a single vector, can be mitigated by contrastive learning."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;X_I&quot;" target="&quot;X_J&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Elements 'x_i' and 'x_j' show interaction within a dataset during training for vector space manipulation tasks like embedding. This indicates collaborative data processing steps."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-347ee1cddb180db47da74eed2ab0a716</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LEARNED ENCODER F&quot;" target="&quot;DATA REPRESENTATION&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Encoder \(f\) outputs data representations that are invariant to certain transformations"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b0b14070bcd3ef6a571246548a4ac62f</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBJECT-VERB-OBJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The subject-verb-object sentence structure could be analogous to the way transformer architectures process inputs. The analogy considers a head of the transformer as an independent filter similar to those in CNNs."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a9d25ca1f54266a4aaf1d699e09c517a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES&quot;" target="&quot;MULTIPLE HEADS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The multiple heads within transformer architectures are compared to filters used in CNNs, highlighting their role in processing data"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a9d25ca1f54266a4aaf1d699e09c517a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBJECT-VERB-ADJECTIVE-SUBJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The analogy between subject-verb-adjective-subject sentence structures and the operation of transformer architectures is based on the description of how queries, keys, and values are processed through weight matrices."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a9d25ca1f54266a4aaf1d699e09c517a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TRANSFORMER ARCHITECTURES&quot;" target="&quot;SUBJECT-VERB-ADVERB-OBJECT&quot;">
      <data key="d4">5.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"This phrase could be used to describe an action that occurs in a block within the transformer architecture, like delivering outputs from attention functions."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a9d25ca1f54266a4aaf1d699e09c517a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CNNS&quot;" target="&quot;MULTIPLE FILTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The concept of multiple filters within CNNs is similar to the analogy made with transformer architectures' heads, emphasizing their role in data filtering."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a9d25ca1f54266a4aaf1d699e09c517a</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;F_\ELL&quot;" target="&quot;CLIP MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Similarly, f_\ell (image encoder) also interacts with the CLIP model to ensure that matching images are closely mapped in the shared embedding space when compared to texts.</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f9c25475041383298d36cd42b4c4750c</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AWS RE:INFORCE 2019&quot;" target="&quot;LOGICAL REASONING TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"At the AWS re:Inforce 2019 event, discussions and demonstrations of logical reasoning technology took place, highlighting its importance in advancements."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e44b4ecdca26910eec0b2588bec56464</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AWS RE:INFORCE 2019&quot;" target="&quot;WORLD MODELS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"At AWS re:Inforce 2019, discussions on World Models were part of the agenda focused on advancing automated reasoning technologies."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e44b4ecdca26910eec0b2588bec56464</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LINEAR TRANSFORMATION OF THE INPUT EMBEDDINGS&quot;" target="&quot;PROJECTION MATRIX W&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"A projection matrix \(W\) is used for linear transformation on input embeddings to achieve location awareness and function awareness."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-301d9df64cefccac5cd2ea7387e7e7e1</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;DATA TENSOR X&quot;" target="&quot;MULTIPLE VIEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Multiple views refer to different representations or aspects of the total data tensor \(\mathbf{X}\), as illustrated in Figure 2."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d51ce3fbf4b4cbff3abd80c83b13839</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;INSPIRED BY&quot;" target="&quot;TIAN ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Figure 2 draws inspiration from Tian et al.'s work on contrastive learning."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d51ce3fbf4b4cbff3abd80c83b13839</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELBO&quot;" target="&quot;KL(Q(\MATHBF Z | \MATHBF X ; \MATHBF \PHI) || P(\MATHBF Z | \MATHBF \THETA))&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The tightness of ELBO bound is represented by the closeness of KL divergence, indicating optimization in data generation process."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2f642986e3cd0cdd9951f94adfb0f5eb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ELBO&quot;" target="&quot;LOG LIKELIHOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Maximizing ELBO optimizes both marginal log likelihood for data generation and minimizes KL divergence for better approximation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2f642986e3cd0cdd9951f94adfb0f5eb</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;PREDICTIVE LEARNING&quot;" target="&quot;SPLITTING A VIDEO INTO PAST AND FUTURE FRAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Predictive Learning techniques involve splitting media content, like videos, to facilitate prediction tasks."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-114ad13da3f029831d24b941874b57f7</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ATTENTION MECHANISM&quot;" target="&quot;MATRIX \(W^Q&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Matrix \(W^q\) is central in the attention mechanism alongside \(W^k\) and \(W^v\) for creating query vectors that are used to dynamically weigh input tokens based on their relevance or importance."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bbe1fa761a3018b797f95e8931d7781d</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;VISUAL CONTENT&quot;" target="&quot;ICONS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Visual elements from images are represented using icons which reflect the color and shape depicted in the image data."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5edf01cab6c5efd1ae75e8d20f662d03</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;COLOR-BASED GROUPING&quot;" target="&quot;EARLY LAYERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Early processing stages in an image encoder typically involve grouping based on color attributes."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5edf01cab6c5efd1ae75e8d20f662d03</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;SHAPE-BASED GROUPING&quot;" target="&quot;LATER LAYERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"Subsequent layers might focus more on shape for advanced feature extraction, contributing to the overall understanding of visual content."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5edf01cab6c5efd1ae75e8d20f662d03</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;KL DIVERGENCE&quot;" target="&quot;DNN_{ENC}&quot;">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"The DNN_{enc} network utilizes KL divergence for optimization of its approximation."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-34a74edcbc6d7e678b64dc5b04afded5</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CEO JOHN SMITH&quot;" target="&quot;WORKS_FOR&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"ABC Inc."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-10dbddedac13c53187f19bbcb3156378</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WORKS_FOR&quot;" target="&quot;CFO JANE DOE&quot;">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"DEF Corp."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-10dbddedac13c53187f19bbcb3156378</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EARLY LAYERS&quot;" target="&quot;LATER LAYERS&quot;">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">"In the context of neural networks, early layers tend to group images by color and later layers group more by shape, reflecting changes in feature extraction throughout deep learning models."</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5edf01cab6c5efd1ae75e8d20f662d03</data>
      <data key="d7">1</data>
    </edge>
